{"slug":"tuples-with-same-product","title":"Four Numbers With Equal Products","topic":"hashing","difficulty":"hard","order":298,"tags":["hashing","hash-map","counting","combinatorics"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Count the pairs of every product, then pair up the pairs","body":["Count the tuples `(a, b, c, d)` of **four different elements** with `a * b = c * d`. Instead of four nested loops, compute the product of **every pair** of elements (`n^2 / 2` pairs) and count in a map how many pairs give each product. Two different pairs with the same product `p` form a valid combination: if `x * y = z * w`, then `x, y, z, w` are four different numbers, because all elements are different (a shared element would force the partners to be equal).",{"code":"prod = {}\nfor i in range(n):\n    for j in range(i + 1, n):\n        p = a[i] * a[j]\n        prod[p] = prod.get(p, 0) + 1\ntotal = sum(8 * c * (c - 1) // 2 for c in prod.values())"},"A group of `c` pairs with the same product contains `c * (c - 1) / 2` couples of pairs. Each couple `{x, y}`, `{z, w}` gives **8 tuples**: choose which pair is first (2 ways), and the order inside each pair (2 and 2 ways)."]},"statement":["You are given `n` different positive integers. Count the tuples `(a, b, c, d)` of four different elements of the array (taken from four different positions) with `a * b = c * d`. The order inside the tuple matters."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n`.","The second line has `n` different integers."],"outputFormat":["Print the number of tuples."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 1000","1 <= each number <= 10^4","All numbers are different."],"examples":[{"input":"4\n2 3 4 6\n","output":"8\n","note":"2 * 6 = 3 * 4: the pairs {2, 6} and {3, 4} give 8 tuples."}],"hints":["Compute the product of every pair of elements.","Count how many pairs have each product.","A product with `c` pairs gives `c * (c - 1) / 2` couples of pairs, and each couple gives 8 tuples."],"starter":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <unordered_map>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["All pair products are counted in a map. Every two pairs with the same product (they cannot share an element) give 8 tuples, so a product with `c` pairs contributes `8 * c * (c - 1) / 2`."],"complexity":"Time O(n^2) on average, space O(n^2).","code":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nprod = {}\nfor i in range(n):\n    for j in range(i + 1, n):\n        p = a[i] * a[j]\n        prod[p] = prod.get(p, 0) + 1\nprint(sum(8 * c * (c - 1) // 2 for c in prod.values()))\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <unordered_map>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    unordered_map<long long, long long> prod;\n    prod.reserve(n * n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) prod[a[i] * a[j]]++;\n    }\n    long long total = 0;\n    for (auto& entry : prod) total += 8 * entry.second * (entry.second - 1) / 2;\n    cout << total << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        Map<Long, Long> prod = new HashMap<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) prod.merge(a[i] * a[j], 1L, Long::sum);\n        }\n        long total = 0;\n        for (long c : prod.values()) total += 8 * c * (c - 1) / 2;\n        System.out.println(total);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"4\n2 3 4 6\n","output":"8\n"},{"input":"1\n5\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"4\n1 2 4 8\n","output":"8\n"},{"input":"4\n2 3 5 7\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"20\n5 40 28 19 18 42 25 37 48 9 16 33 10 31 1 56 46 47 12 13\n","output":"64\n"},{"input":"300\n185 584 934 1482 1782 1528 1472 859 1369 75 176 928 1195 497 681 1572 549 1766 642 1025 1628 647 555 914 666 1700 1635 1026 1309 618 187 498 885 74 1391 1748 1230 1034 206 819 257 1928 1515 320 477 768 722 966 600 823 434 1604 301 1958 1401 469 1419 1056 1210 1035 68 249 1902 1159 1509 1856 638 40 839 1053 919 405 1830 974 1549 303 230 364 1689 1946 1952 234 1310 296 658 1735 1468 70 404 1815 903 442 144 194 1566 927 1619 482 3 282 212 662 958 699 1393 1001 1730 29 93 581 132 471 1343 535 962 1457 1609 27 583 1705 861 585 1516 1739 1682 1578 605 100 953 69 525 1146 1864 1466 876 622 1956 1618 1003 183 418 1214 1384 1583 1322 1883 1758 516 1442 621 1029 1451 1436 1120 22 1098 278 1979 499 941 1264 1289 396 452 1706 1300 1887 445 72 1925 564 1650 1288 1114 410 548 1130 1745 1241 315 64 1612 1327 890 711 848 346 122 1123 690 1511 1125 1927 1184 1281 81 26 794 191 1193 1625 1813 407 136 682 400 1316 977 1632 215 453 976 1199 771 149 49 1675 1268 1231 1081 1041 1785 956 881 1581 2000 860 541 470 15 1521 767 419 342 359 1274 91 285 696 1506 1080 522 1749 1235 1494 247 1365 1779 610 197 695 1261 590 519 196 21 1713 670 117 1204 1778 961 1920 1425 101 1982 637 572 1381 805 1283 443 1584 378 1998 137 1776 503 753 997 714 269 1795 1733 539 1756 1221 1209 1373 51 894 1918 199 933 1325 992 1640 620 205 1726\n","output":"13960\n"},{"input":"1